ost intense sequences  this dangerous region houses the maul  cluster the home of the beast that  nearly swallows the millennium falcon  hole during han solo and his crew's  perilous attempt to make the famed  kessel run  they of course make it in less than 12  parsecs as long as you round down  speaking of solo the red-skinned alien  who plants a tracker on the razer crest  is a mim-van zee a species first  introduced in the standalone prequel  flick  with a child presumably safe at school  and the razor crest in for a tune-up  grief mando and kara head back to  grief's office to talk business  the moment they walk in the door they're  greeted by mithril who now lives a life  of servitude to make up for getting on  grief's bad side  this is the same character mando took  the bounty on and frozen carbonite in  the mandalorians premiere episode  despite having thought some time ago  mithril complains of a very familiar  side effect that comes with prolonged  carbon freezing  grief makes sure to let mithral know he  has no qualms about sticking him back on  ice should he not follow his directions  to which the blue alien remarks that he  prefer not to and that he still can't  see out of his left eye  this refers back to return of the jedi  in which han solo's release from  carbonite established the existence of  hibernation sickness  an ailment that presents itself as  temporary blindness depending on the  length of one's imprisonment  the team wastes little time to party  navarro for the outlying imperial base  on the installation's upper level cara  mando and grief assess their situation  and review the plan while mithril stands  on  what will become their one-way ticket  off the sabotaged base a trexel marauder  this vehicle which appears to be a  variation of an imperial troop transport  has popped up in a few star wars  projects lately including star wars  rebels  but it took over four decades to get the  vehicle in live action  this particular people movers roots go  all the way back to the toy stores of  1978  where the imperial troop transport  arrived as part of kenner star wars  action figure line  so mithril's excitement at finding a  quote mint trexel marauder is likely a  nod to the vehicle's toy store origins  surprisingly the mission to rid navarro  of imperial presence goes off without a  hitch  the crew manages to make a fairly clean  getaway but not before they uncover a  disturbing secret about why the empire  is so interested in the child  by the looks of things the imperial  remnant is going all in and trying to  perfect a way to clone a force-sensitive  beam  a hologram message from dr pershing  explains the empire's dire need for the  child's blood if they are to keep this  mysterious program going  he also mentions the child's m count  likely referring to the amount of many  chlorines in his body that contribute to  his proficiency in the force  many chlorines have remained one of the  most controversial parts of the star  wars universe since their debut in the  phantom menace and fans haven't heard  them discussed in the franchise for  quite some time  so what does this all mean this  fledgling imperial cloning  program could connect the mysteriously  alive emperor palpatine and his tanks  full of snoke clones  the rise of skywalker established that  palpatine spent years biding his time on  hexagonal and rapidly decaying bodies  attempting to find the path to  immortality through cloning  the remnants of his empire could have  been hard at work trying to create a new  more powerful form for their leader  during the events of the mandalorian  considering how strong yoda and the  child species is in the force and the  length of their natural lifespan there's  no better candidate for a sith lord  who's trying to rule the galaxy for all  time with absolute power  but there's also another possibility at  the very end of the siege mop gideon  admires a whole room full of large black  stormtrooper-like figures  what are those supposed to be the audio  description on disney plus has the  answer  calling them immobilized dark troopers  dark troopers first popped up in the  1995 first person shooter game star wars  dark forces where it's implied that  they're droids  and the word immobilized does suggest  that gideon and his technician are  tending to a fleet to power down bots  but dark troopers have also been  described as cyborgs and other star wars  media meaning gideon could be preparing  exo suits for future force-sensitive  clone bodies to occupy  dark troopers also appear in the dark  empire series of comics as elite  stormtroopers who have received horse  training so this could also be the  destiny gideon has in mind for the  clones  after all if they're just droids why  wouldn't gideon have already deployed  them  perhaps he's waiting for a batch of  powerful force users to bring the suits  to life  and that's the whole point of dr  pershing's mysterious cloning project  whatever they turn out to be they're  probably bad news  mando had better be ready check out one  of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  mandalorian are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

